    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0259" n="889" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg889"/>

                <head>No. 386.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="from">Fish</persName> to General <persName corresp="#p_DES1"
                            type="to">Sickles</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-02-12"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 12,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>So soon as the republican government is fully established and in possession of
                    the power of the nation you will recognize it. You will not fail to urge upon a
                    government already committed to the principles and the expediency of
                    emancipation and of political reforms the immediate enforcement of practical and
                    efficient reforms and the abolition of slavery in the colonies. The present
                    seems to be the moment when the government can accomplish great results.
                    Endeavor to have the decrees self-acting, and not dependent upon future
                    regulations, which have always proved inoperative and reactionary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_HF1">FISH</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
